@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:b380a5ca16c986d6b527c7bf74bad3eb605b899e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It now goes in the JSON as a `behind` field, and on stdout only in the human-readable mode where it belongs." }
~ `stale --json` now includes the `behind` field in JSON output instead of printing it on stdout.

To ensure that `--json` outputs only valid JSON, the `behind` information was moved from stdout to the JSON object. This prevents parsing errors when consuming the JSON output.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:b380a5ca16c986d6b527c7bf74bad3eb605b899e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A test runs every `--json` command in this repository, which records its own commits, and requires the output to parse." }
~ A test is added to ensure that every `--json` command produces valid JSON output.

To catch future regressions where non-JSON content might be printed with `--json`, a test was added that checks the validity of the JSON output.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if let Some(mut around) = scope {" }
~ The `facts` function now includes an optional `scope` parameter to filter facts based on files, names, or …

To provide more granular control over which facts are displayed, the `facts` function was updated to accept a `scope` parameter that allows filtering by specific criteria.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.estimate {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now estimates the time required for extraction based on commit size and prints …

To give users an idea of how long the extraction process will take, especially when processing multiple commits, an estimation feature was added.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if dry_run {" }
~ The `extract` function now includes a dry-run mode that simulates the extraction process without actually …

To allow users to preview what would be extracted without making any changes, a dry-run mode was added to the `extract` function.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if let Some(path) = c.prompt_file {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `prompt_file` parameter that allows specifying a custom system …

To provide more flexibility in how the check process is conducted, the `check` function was updated to accept a `prompt_file` parameter for customizing the system prompt.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let take = if r.max_commits == 0 {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `max_commits` parameter to limit the number of commits processed …

To prevent processing an excessive number of commits at once, which could be resource-intensive, a `max_commits` parameter was added to limit the number of commits processed.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let kept = if force {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `force` parameter to force re-extraction of already recorded …

To allow users to re-extract commits that have already been recorded, a `force` parameter was added to the `extract_command` function.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.dry_run {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `dry_run` parameter to simulate the extraction process without …

To allow users to preview what would be extracted without making any changes, a dry-run mode was added to the `extract_command` function.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let mut settings = Settings {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `no_corpus_order` parameter that allows disabling corpus order …

To provide more flexibility in how the check process is conducted, the `check` function was updated to accept a `no_corpus_order` parameter for disabling corpus order.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.queued {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `queued` parameter to handle extraction of commits from a queue.

To allow users to extract commits that have been queued, either by the post-commit hook or manually, a `queued` parameter was added to the `extract_command` function.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let mut settings = Settings {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `parts` parameter to specify the maximum number of parts for …

To allow users to control how the change is split into parts during the checking process, a `parts` parameter was added to the `check` function.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/tests/cargo_subcommand.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": `--json` puts JSON on stdout and nothing else. }
~ `--json` must be JSON, and nothing else

CI went red on a corpus that had grown enough for the case to arise: `stale --json` printed which decisions each moved item was behind — on stdout, before the JSON — and anything reading the output got `Expecting value: line 1 column 3`.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/tests/cargo_subcommand.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It did not: a later change printed which decisions each moved item was behind, on stdout, before the JSON — so anything reading the output got a parse error." }
~ It now goes in the JSON as a `behind` field

That line came in with the anchors and was never run with `--json` on a corpus that had any. It now goes in the JSON as a `behind` field, and on stdout only in the human-readable mode where it belongs.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/tests/cargo_subcommand.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It did not: a later change printed which decisions each moved item was behind, on stdout, before the JSON — so anything reading the output got a parse error." }
~ On stdout only in the human-readable mode

That line came in with the anchors and was never run with `--json` on a corpus that had any. It now goes in the JSON as a `behind` field, and on stdout only in the human-readable mode where it belongs.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:b380a5ca16c986d6b527c7bf74bad3eb605b899e }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A test runs every `--json` command in this repository, which records its own commits, and requires the output to parse." }
~ A test runs every `--json` command in this repository

A test runs every `--json` command in this repository, which records its own commits, and requires the output to parse. It would have caught this one, and it is the only thing that would: the human output was correct throughout.

@decision d/gb380a5ca16c9-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/tests/cargo_subcommand.rs@b380a5ca16c9 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": `cargo_finds_and_runs_the_subcommand` }
~ `cargo_finds_and_runs_the_subcommand`

The tool must work as an external cargo subcommand, so these tests go through real `cargo`, with the directory of the built `cargo-smysl` first on PATH, as `cargo install` would leave it.

